<section>
  <div class="wrap two two--top">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Every morning</p>
      <h2>Three lessons, and all of them in English</h2>
      <p>We are an English language center, and this is how we teach the language: English, Maths and Science before lunch every day, following Cambridge Primary, every lesson in English. The subject gives your child something worth saying, and the words come with it. A child who can tell you why the shape rolled instead of stacking has just used English for something real.</p>
      <h3>English</h3>
      <p>The lesson where the language itself is the subject: phonics, reading, writing and a lot of talking. Real books, a book corner, and a story on the rug.</p>
      <h3>Maths</h3>
      <p>Starts with the objects — counters, dice, bingo cards, shapes cut from paper — and with the words that go with them: more than, fewer, half, heavier, roll or stack. Children say what they did and how they know it, then write it down.</p>
      <h3>Science</h3>
      <p>Experiments first, explanations second. Children guess out loud, watch what happens and put it into words: first, then, because, it changed. Naming what you saw is the hard part, and it is the English part.</p>
      <p>Cambridge Primary is recognised everywhere, so moving on later is easy, and the English your child builds here goes with them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="leaf-wrap leaf-wrap--r has-sticker">
      <span class="sticker sticker--green sticker--tr">Cambridge Primary</span>
      {% photo "primary-english-lesson", "photo--lg photo--tall photo--tilt-r" %}
    </div>
  </div>
